When?

259
00:14:49,681 --> 00:14:51,683
February 14, 1982.

260
00:14:52,267 --> 00:14:55,961
I was 23 months old, it was Valentine's day, and mom and dad went out for dinner.

261
00:14:56,646 --> 00:14:58,273
You were there. Don't you remember?

262
00:15:03,445 --> 00:15:04,654
I got nothing.

263
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:07,115
You can really remember when you were that little?

264
00:15:07,324 --> 00:15:08,575
Uh-huh. You were there, too.

265
00:15:08,784 --> 00:15:10,584
You were still struggling with potty training.

266
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:12,245
I don't think so.

267
00:15:12,454 --> 00:15:15,582
Oh, yes. Meemaw used to call you Mr. Soggy pants.

268
00:15:15,791 --> 00:15:16,541
Nuh-uh.

269
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:18,251
Uaughsy Mr. Soggy pants.

270
00:15:18,460 --> 00:15:19,961
Quit it. This is serious.

271
00:15:20,170 --> 00:15:22,005
Sheldon, you've got to tell dad that recipe.

272
00:15:22,506 --> 00:15:24,758
But meemaw told me it was a secret.

273
00:15:24,966 --> 00:15:27,719
If you don't, and mom and dad get a divorce, it's your fault.

274
00:15:29,346 --> 00:15:30,055
All right.

275
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:31,263
Fine.

276
00:15:32,808 --> 00:15:34,810
Good job, soggy pants.

277
00:15:37,604 --> 00:15:39,981
Dad, could you please come into the living room?

278
00:15:40,524 --> 00:15:41,524
What for?

279
00:15:41,566 --> 00:15:44,569
My brain did something impressive and I'd like to share it with you.

280
00:15:46,029 --> 00:15:47,322
Hmm.

281
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:54,579
What are you doing here?

282
00:15:54,996 --> 00:15:56,123
Same as you.

283
00:15:56,331 --> 00:15:58,125
I want to see what his brain did.

284
00:15:58,333 --> 00:15:59,418
Please have a seat.

285
00:16:01,378 --> 00:16:02,587
All right.

286
00:16:06,216 --> 00:16:07,216
George sr.: Well?

287
00:16:07,509 --> 00:16:09,553
I know meemaw's brisket recipe.

288
00:16:09,845 --> 00:16:10,470
What?

289
00:16:10,679 --> 00:16:11,471
No, you don't.

290
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,140
Yes, I do.

291
00:16:13,348 --> 00:16:16,935
And in order to bring peace to this family, I'm prepared to make it public.

292
00:16:17,144 --> 00:16:17,936
You're bluffing.

293
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:22,774
One tablespoon of cumin, one cup of brown sugar, two tablespoons of smoked paprika...

294
00:16:22,983 --> 00:16:23,983
Okay, okay, stop.

295
00:16:24,109 --> 00:16:25,109
No, no, no. Keep going.

296
00:16:25,152 --> 00:16:26,778
How do you know the recipe, Shelly?

297
00:16:26,987 --> 00:16:29,823
Meemaw told it to me on Valentine's day, 1982.

298
00:16:30,031 --> 00:16:33,160
You were out with dad seeing cannonball run at the dollar theater.

299
00:16:33,368 --> 00:16:35,662
That's impossible, you weren't even two years old.

300
00:16:35,871 --> 00:16:39,082
Three tablespoons of dried mustard, one cup of lone star beer...

301
00:16:39,291 --> 00:16:40,291
Okay.

302
00:16:41,918 --> 00:16:42,918
Okay.

303
00:16:43,879 --> 00:16:45,046
Go ahead.

304
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:47,174
Give it to your father.

305
00:16:47,466 --> 00:16:49,009
I can write it down for you.

306
00:16:50,969 --> 00:16:52,345
That's okay, I don't want it.

307
00:16:52,554 --> 00:16:54,764
You have got to be kidding me.

308
00:16:54,973 --> 00:16:59,495
Connie, you've had every opportunity to give me that recipe and you never did, because you've always treated me like an outsider.

309
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:00,312
No, she has not.

310
00:17:00,520 --> 00:17:01,605
Oh, of course I have.

311
00:17:01,813 --> 00:17:02,981
See? She admits it.

312
00:17:03,398 --> 00:17:05,025
Damn right, I do.

313
00:17:05,775 --> 00:17:07,986
Never thought you were good enough for my daughter.

314
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:12,115
There you were, riding around on that dumb motorcycle, knocking her up.

315
00:17:12,324 --> 00:17:15,312
Why don't you kids go in the kitchen and fix yourselves some ice cream?

316
00:17:15,494 --> 00:17:16,995
I'm not going anywhere.

317
00:17:19,331 --> 00:17:21,208
Hey. I get it.

318
00:17:22,334 --> 00:17:23,502
I have a daughter.

319
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,338
I wouldn't want her bringing home someone like that.

320
00:17:28,006 --> 00:17:30,258
But I've come a hell of a long way since then.

321
00:17:34,304 --> 00:17:35,764
Okay, you're right.

322
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:41,560
George.

323
00:17:43,855 --> 00:17:45,106
I'm sorry.

324
00:17:48,235 --> 00:17:50,904
That means more to me than any recipe.

325
00:17:52,614 --> 00:17:53,657
Come here.

326
00:18:01,164 --> 00:18:02,767
Don't let the hug fool you.

327
00:18:02,791 --> 00:18:06,127
The minute she went home, he made me give him the recipe.

328
00:18:09,923 --> 00:18:13,009
Here we go, maiden voyage.

329
00:18:15,220 --> 00:18:17,055
Mmm, mmm.

330
00:18:17,264 --> 00:18:18,515
Hot damn.

331
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:21,184
George sr.: Hot damn.

332
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:26,439
Hot damn!

333
00:18:26,648 --> 00:18:28,984
George! Language.

334
00:18:29,317 --> 00:18:30,317
Sheldon.

335
00:18:30,986 --> 00:18:31,986
Want some?

336
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:34,573
Uh, no, thank you. I'm not hungry.
